+# Bug Assessment: Product review privacy, validation, authorization, and rating integrity
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Created**: 2026-11-18T00:00:00+00:00
+- **Source**: pasted text
+- **Verdict**: valid
+- **Severity**: high
+
+## Report (verbatim or summarized)
+
+The ticket reports that public product reviews expose the reviewer's email and home address; duplicate customer reviews and ratings of 9 return server errors; and merchant edits/deletions do not update product ratings. The required behavior specifies a privacy-safe public DTO, 1–5 whole-number validation, 409 duplicate reviews, 403 customer-id mismatch, 404 merchant review/product mismatches, and recalculated one-decimal half-up product averages/counts after add/update/delete.
+
+## Symptom
+
+The current product-review API leaks a full readable customer object, returns 500/503 for client validation cases, does not enforce that the authenticated customer owns the submitted customer id, and updates product ratings incrementally on every save without correcting edits or deletes. Product rating presentation also uses the wrong rounding behavior and can retain stale values.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+1. GET `/api/v1/product/{id}/reviews` for a product with a review and inspect the serialized customer object.
+2. POST `/api/v1/auth/products/{id}/reviews` with a duplicate customer/product or rating `9`; observe the current 500/503 handling.
+3. POST with a customer id different from the logged-in customer; observe that the request is not rejected by ownership authorization.
+4. PUT or DELETE `/api/v1/private/products/{id}/reviews/{reviewId}` and then GET `/api/v2/product/{sku}`; observe that the aggregate is not recomputed from the remaining reviews.
+
+## Suspected Code Paths
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/product/ProductReviewApi.java` — product-review POST/PUT/DELETE handlers manually emit 500/503 responses, use a broad customer DTO for public reads, and do not consistently validate resource ownership.
+- `sm-shop-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/model/catalog/product/ReadableProductReview.java` — public response contains `ReadableCustomer`, whose inherited fields include customer contact/address data.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/catalog/ReadableProductReviewPopulator.java` — populates the full `ReadableCustomer` into each public review.
+- `sm-shop-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/model/catalog/product/ProductReviewEntity.java` — rating is `Double` with `@Min/@Max`, allowing fractional ratings rather than requiring a whole number.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/product/review/ProductReviewServiceImpl.java` — aggregate is adjusted by adding the incoming rating and count, with no recalculation for update/delete and no zero-review reset.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/catalog/product/ReadableProductMapper.java` — product rating is rounded to half-star increments rather than one decimal place using half-up rounding.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/repositories/catalog/product/review/ProductReviewRepository.java` — existing product/customer lookup supports duplicate detection but needs safe use for rejected requests and aggregate recomputation.
+
+## Root Cause Hypothesis
+
+Confidence: high. The public DTO directly embeds a populated `ReadableCustomer`; the API catches all exceptions and converts expected client errors to 500/503; the review entity has no whole-number constraint and the controller does not compare the submitted customer id with the authenticated principal; and `ProductReviewServiceImpl.saveOrUpdate` treats every save as a new review while delete delegates to the generic repository without updating the product. The aggregate mapper further applies half-star rounding instead of the requested one-decimal half-up rule.
+
+## Proposed Remediation
+
+**Preferred**: Replace the public review customer payload with a minimal reviewer representation containing only the reviewer's first name, while preserving review id, rating, description, date, and the existing product-review response shape. Add whole-number validation (`Integer` or an equivalent integral constraint) and handle invalid ratings as HTTP 400. In the authenticated POST path, compare the submitted customer id with the authenticated customer identity before persistence, return 403 on mismatch, and return 409 for an existing product/customer review. Ensure validation and duplicate/authorization checks occur before any write.
+
+Make merchant PUT/DELETE operate only on the review identified by both path ids and return 404 for absent or cross-product reviews. Centralize product-review aggregate maintenance in the product-review service: after create, update, and delete, load all reviews for the product, compute count and average with `BigDecimal` scale 1 and `RoundingMode.HALF_UP`, and set both to zero when empty. Expose that value in the v2 product mapper without half-star rounding. Add focused unit/API tests for privacy, status codes, ownership, resource scoping, validation, and aggregate transitions.
+
+**Alternatives** (optional):
+- Keep the existing `Double` wire type but add a custom integral validator; this preserves compatibility but is easier to bypass or misunderstand than an integer rating field.
+- Maintain aggregates incrementally with old/new rating deltas and delete decrements; this is more efficient but more fragile than recomputing from the authoritative review rows.
+
+**Files likely to change**:
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/product/ProductReviewApi.java`
+- `sm-shop-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/model/catalog/product/ReadableProductReview.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/catalog/ReadableProductReviewPopulator.java`
+- `sm-shop-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/model/catalog/product/ProductReviewEntity.java`
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/product/review/ProductReviewService.java`
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/product/review/ProductReviewServiceImpl.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/catalog/product/ReadableProductMapper.java`
+- relevant `sm-shop` and `sm-core` review tests
+
+**Tests to add or update**:
+- Public review JSON contains only the permitted reviewer first name and review fields, with no email or address.
+- POST rejects fractional, zero, six, and nine ratings with 400; duplicate reviews return 409; mismatched customer ids return 403; rejected requests leave no new row.
+- Merchant PUT and DELETE return 404 for missing/cross-product reviews and update the aggregate for edit/delete.
+- Add, edit, delete, and remove-last-review cases produce the correct one-decimal half-up average and count in v2 product output.
+
+## Risks & Considerations
+
+- Removing customer fields from the public review JSON is an intentional privacy/API tightening and may affect clients that relied on the leaked payload.
+- Authentication context details must be read using the project’s established security principal conventions; trusting only the request body is not sufficient.
+- Existing persisted aggregate values may be stale; the next review mutation will correct the affected product, while a data repair would be needed for untouched products.
+- Review update must preserve the existing review/customer/product identity and description relationships rather than accidentally inserting a second row.
+
+## Open Questions
+
+- None blocking the requested implementation.
